[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n2_thomas"
text = "# DRAFT
# Thomas at dusk, at his herbs in the infirmary (night 2). He opens, quietly, with the prior about the abbey at night
# (n2_thomas_prior): true, and the prior is innocent. Then the merchant: drowned drunk (his lie), or alive, or turned away.
# The knock with no one there: boys from the lane. Bede's warning about the bread: Bede fasts and sees things.
# Telling him about the bread is the wrong brother (Suspicion +5). Bede is already dead; Thomas knows it.
== start [set n2_thomas_prior]
(Thomas looks past you at the door before he speaks, and keeps his voice low.)
Thomas: Brother. I've seen the prior about the abbey at night. In the court, by the guesthouse, long after Compline.
Thomas: He has no business there at that hour. I don't say what it means. Only, if you see a man in the dark, it may be Hugh.
-> merchant [if died_merchant]
-> lived [if n1_merchant=admitted]
-> refused [if n1_merchant=refused]
-> topics

== merchant
-> merchant_thomas [if reported_merchant=thomas]
-> merchant_prior [if reported_merchant=prior]
-> merchant_plain

== merchant_thomas
Thomas: And the merchant. You did right to come to me this morning, and quietly. Ale and a fishpond: no fault of yours.
-> topics

== merchant_prior
Thomas: And the merchant. You took him to Hugh, I hear. He'll have made it your doing. It wasn't. The man was drunk.
-> topics

== merchant_plain
Thomas: And the merchant. Ale, and a fishpond in the dark. It's no fault of yours, brother. Don't carry him.
-> topics

== lived
Thomas: Your merchant left at first light, cursing the porter who locked him in like a sheep. Well. He's alive to curse.
-> topics

== refused
Thomas: You turned the merchant away. We receive every guest as Christ, the Rule says. Still, it was your first night.
-> topics

== again
(Thomas is back at his mortar.)
Thomas: Brother. Supper soon.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n2_thomas_why] (Ask what the prior would be doing out at night.) -> why
* [if n1_knock_no_one] [if not n2_thomas_knock] (Tell him about the knock with no one there.) -> knock
* [if bread_warned] [if not n2_thomas_bread] (Tell him you were warned off the bread.) -> bread

== why [set n2_thomas_why]
Thomas: I don't know, and I'd rather not guess at a brother's sins.
Thomas: You're up all night. You'll see more than I do. Watch, that's all I ask.
-> topics

== knock [set n2_thomas_knock]
(For a moment he doesn't answer. Then he smiles.)
Thomas: Boys from the lane, knocking and running. They did it to Anselm for years.
Thomas: And Mab sleeps more than she lets on. Don't lose sleep over a knock.
-> topics

== bread [set n2_thomas_bread] [suspicion 5]
Thomas: Bede, was it? I saw him at your ear.
Thomas: Bede fasts till he faints, and then he sees things in the rafters. Eat your bread, brother. You need your strength.
-> topics

== leave
Thomas: Keep it between us, brother. About the prior.
"
